v 3
d suppress. Small-cell suppression for public-release tables.
d
d suppress blanks table cells whose counts fall below a
d disclosure threshold (primary suppression) and, on request,
d blanks the next-smallest cell in each group so that published
d group totals cannot reveal a hidden value by subtraction
d (complementary suppression). It works on plain long-form
d datasets with one observation per table cell, such as the
d output of contract or collapse, and writes publication-ready
d numeric, flag, and string copies of the counts.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or later. No other dependencies.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
d
f suppress.ado
